    "created_at": "2018-03-14T07:07:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-14T07:07:41Z",
    "body": "What you are suggesting is effectively introducing a new element with equivalent semantics to the `template` element. That comes at a high cost and is unlikely to gain support given that it duplicates an element and requires changes to the HTML parser (which have a high bar).\r\n\r\nIf instead the suggestion is changed to make it create an HTML `template` element, but whose insertion mode sticks with SVG somehow, that would already be far more reasonable, but given https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/919#issuecomment-276329905 is also unlikely to succeed.\r\n\r\nI do think it would be good to figure out something here as SVG is very much part of the platform and it's rather crappy for templates to not support it properly, but it's probably better at this point to take a couple steps back and focus on high-level use cases and requirements first (and perhaps a survey of what frameworks have on offer).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
